      "writtenOn": "2022-11-25T18:03:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This could be a struct with two const variants to choose from.\n\nDid you consider using these as macro parameters of a header file? You could have something like:\n\ns2mpu_mpt_template.h:\n```\nstatic bool ARG_PREFIX##_is_smpt_uniform(u32 *smpt, enum mpt_prot prot)\n{\n\tsize_t i;\n\tu64 *doublewords \u003d (u64 *)smpt;\n\tfor (i \u003d 0; i \u003c ARG_SMPT_NUM_WORDS / 2; i++) {\n\t\tif (doublewords[i] !\u003d ARG_LUT_PROT[prot])\n\t\t\treturn false;\n\t}\n\treturn true;\n}\n```  \n\ns2mpu_mpt.c:\n```\n#define ARG_PREFIX          s2mpu_v1\n#define ARG_SMPT_NUM_WORDS  S2MPU_NUM_WORDS(MPT_PROT_BITS)\n#define ARG_LUT_PROT        mpt_prot_doubleword\n#include \"s2mpu_mpt_template.h\"\n#undef ARG_PREFIX\n#undef ARG_SMPT_NUM_WORDS\n#undef ARG_LUT_PROT\n\nconst s2mpu_mpt_ops mpt_ops_v1 \u003d { ... };\n\n#define ARG_PREFIX          s2mpu_v9\n#define ARG_SMPT_NUM_WORDS  S2MPU_NUM_WORDS(V9_MPT_PROT_BITS)\n#define ARG_LUT_PROT        v9_mpt_prot_doubleword\n#include \"s2mpu_mpt_template.h\"\n#undef ARG_PREFIX\n#undef ARG_SMPT_NUM_WORDS\n#undef ARG_LUT_PROT\n\nconst s2mpu_mpt_ops mpt_ops_v9 \u003d { ... };\n```\n\nThat could make the operations faster (benchmark pending).\n\nThe downside is slightly more kernel code, of course, but once we move this to a vendor module, each device\u0027s vendor module would only compile the version it needs.\n\nAnd it would make the selftests easier as well. You\u0027re already doing templating there anyway.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 23,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 26,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "e865d46fec493f4f1689fb793f9f35488fb46c32",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
