      "writtenOn": "2022-11-28T16:36:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I though about it, I saw it will add more memory and as the new variables should be loaded in the beginning of the function and there are a lot of iterations accessing memory, I didn\u0027t think it will differ much.\n\nI tried this now\nDifference in MicrodroidBenchmarks:\nMost of parameters are the nearly the same.\nnoticeable changes in bootloader_time_average_ms[protectedVM\u003dtrue]. for template, time decreases from 0.7243 to 0.6145\n\nDifference in Size(vmlinux): when using template, .text size increased from 0x141E188 to 0x141F188 (4K)\n\nIf this trade-off is acceptable I can add a new patch with templating",
